course: dictionary
lesson: 3564
title: Fertile
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one fits. Look for the clues before you decide. «Floods spread mud on flat land beside the river, making a fertile flood plain.» Mud and rivers suggest land that is good for growing things, so fertile here means good for growing crops.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The steppes of Ukraine have very fertile black soil.» If you swap in good for growing crops and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right. If it sounds silly, look for another meaning.
explain: The same word can work in a different way. «A fertile imagination» has nothing to do with soil. Fertile here means full of new ideas. The word after it, imagination, is the clue that tells you which meaning the author means.
fact: Fertile means good for growing plants and crops.
fact: «Fertile soil» and «fertile land» are rich enough to help farming grow well.
fact: «The black soils of Ukraine, called chernozem, are among the most fertile in the world.»
fact: «A fertile imagination» means a mind with lots of new ideas.
fact: Fertile can also describe animals, people and seeds that can have babies or grow.
exercise: «The black soils of Ukraine are among the most fertile in the world.» What does fertile mean here? | Full of stones | Cold and icy | *Good for growing crops | Very dark in colour
exercise: Mia says a fertile imagination is about soil. What does it really mean? | Land that grows wheat | *A mind full of lots of new ideas | Dark and damp | A deep hole in the ground
exercise: «Most people live in river valleys, coastal plains and fertile lowlands.» Why do people choose fertile lowlands to live? | Because the land is covered in ice | *Because the land is good for growing food | Because the mountains are too warm | Because there are no roads
exercise: Find and copy one word that means good for growing crops in «Floods spread mud on flat land, making a fertile flood plain.» | mud | flat | flood | *fertile
test: Which phrase describes a mind with lots of new ideas? | Fertile lowlands by the sea | Fertile soil near the river | *A fertile imagination | Fertile land for wheat
test: «The Fertile Crescent» is a name for an area of rich land. What is the clue that it is good land? | The word land, which means a country | The word crescent, which means a shape of a moon | *The word fertile, which means good for growing crops | It is a name for a desert
exam: «Egypt is a country where almost everyone lives in the thin green strip along the Nile.» Why is the strip green and crowded with people? | Because the sand is too hot to walk on | *Because the land beside the river is fertile and good for growing crops | Because people prefer deserts | Because the Nile is frozen
